sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Worker as Priority worker
    participant TC as TypeCheckEnv / finalize
    participant ST as SharedState.symbol_tables
    participant TP as SharedState.typecheck_products
    participant Sched as CompileScheduler
    participant Reader as Import fast path / REPL / codegen reader

    Note over Worker,Reader: Current state: symbol publication and readiness are separate mechanisms coupled by convention.

    Worker->>TC: check form / finalize module
    TC->>ST: create or update symbol-table entries
    Worker->>TP: insert typecheck product
    Worker->>Sched: notify_typecheck_done(module)

    alt Fast-path reader
        Reader->>Sched: is_typechecked(module)?
        Sched-->>Reader: yes
        Reader->>ST: read symbol-table entries
    else Nice/codegen reader
        Reader->>Sched: take_object_codegen / claim ready module
        Reader->>TP: read typecheck product
        Reader->>ST: read symbol table for names / code
    end

    Note over ST,Sched: The scheduler does not own the payload, only the readiness flag/pool state.
    Note over Worker,Reader: Correctness depends on the writer completing symbol publication before the scheduler transition becomes observable.
    Note over ST: This is the core publish-then-read surface behind the observed import race.
